Z||000000||Shaun41178||12-23-2001||05:43 PM||||Since I needed to get a couple of bolts to mount my gen 3 on the engine stand I thought I would share with you the size bolts that you will need to purchase for use with an engine stand.  Length will vary pending on what type of engine stand you use.  I had used 4.5 inch long before and this time I needed 3.5<P>just thought I would let everyone know to save some headache.  Oh yes dont' forget a couple of washers<P>------------------<BR>SOLD 85 GT w/ nitrous.<BR>Looking for another.<BR>FOR SALE: Aluminum v6 block.<BR>Shaun41178@hotmail.com<BR>PORN FOREVER!||||reg||1
Z||000001||FieroJoe||12-23-2001||06:01 PM||||I just put my newly acquired V6 on a AC Delco stand I bought at Murray's.  The stand was $50, and isnt the cheapo 3 wheel type, its got four solid wheels so it wont tip over easily.<P>The bolts I needed were the 12 x1.75, and I got some 100mm ones that worked out great.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/end2.jpg"> <P>Theres a pic, don't worry, it will be all cleaned up nice and painted before I swap it in!||||reg||1
